    "title": "March Madness schedule, TV channels, how to watch Elite 8 basketball",
    "text": "March 26, 2026Updated March 28, 2026, 8:37 a.m. MTThe 2026 NCAA Tournament is down to eight teams remaining.The Elite Eight round of March Madness on Saturday, March 28, and Sunday, March 29, offers some very interesting games to watch on television or streaming.Here's a look at the TV information for each Elite Eight NCAA Tournament men's basketball game, with the teams, scheduled game time, channel and streaming information.All times MST (add three hours for Eastern time).The winners of the Elite Eight games advance to the Final Four round on Saturday, April 4.How to watch Elite 8 games: Iowa vs Illinois | Purdue vs Arizona | Tennessee vs Michigan | UConn vs Duke | Schedule | Announcers | Who is in Elite 8?Watch NCAA Tournament games on Sling TVSaturday's March Madness schedule: Elite Eight games3:09 p.m.: No. 9 Iowa vs No. 3 Illinois, TBS/truTV (stream with Sling TV)5:49 p.m.: No. 2 Purdue vs No. 1 Arizona, TBS/truTV (stream with Sling TV)March Madness Elite 8 odds: Iowa vs Illinois | Purdue vs Arizona | Tennessee vs Michigan | UConn vs Duke | Betting odds | National championship oddsSunday's March Madness schedule: Elite Eight games11:15 a.m.: No. 6 Tennessee vs No. 1 Michigan, CBS (stream with FUBO)2:05 p.m.: No. 2 UConn vs No. 1 Duke, CBS (stream with FUBO)March Madness Elite 8 picks: Iowa vs Illinois | Purdue vs Arizona | Tennessee vs Michigan | UConn vs Duke | The Republic's predictionsReach Jeremy Cluff at jeremy.cluff@arizonarepublic.com. Follow him on X, formerly Twitter @Jeremy_Cluff.Support local journalism: Subscribe to azcentral.com today. Sign up for azcentral Preps Now. And be sure to subscribe to our daily sports newsletters so you don't miss a thing.Our team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.",
